28np|n|One who, or that which, whisks, or moves with a quick, sweeping motion. ; Formerly, the hair of the upper lip; a mustache; -- usually in the plural. ; That part of the beard which grows upon the sides of the face, or upon the chin, or upon both; as, side whiskers; chin whiskers. ; A hair of the beard. ; One of the long, projecting hairs growing at the sides of the mouth of a cat, or other animal. ; Iron rods extending on either side of the bowsprit, to spread, or guy out, the stays, etc.	a:1ta1,14,2;1e3p,4,2~1e3p,4,2;1ta1,14,2	v:zc,19,5;1e3p,10,3;26ev,0,4~zc,19,5;26ev,0,4;1e3p,10,3	N:18ye,83,313;1843,52,6;f6m,36,3;ze8,31,4~18ye,83,313;1843,52,6;ze8,31,4;f6m,36,3
